  "frozenPublicHeadObligations": [
    {
      "id": "A01",
      "line": 24,
      "reason": "Actual strict positive-prefix event and actual supplied Brownian probability; real sSup on exact open window Ioo (a n) 1; no probability assumption unnecessarily added to the transparent definition."
    },
    {
      "id": "A02",
      "line": 33,
      "reason": "For every n>0 and every real boundary, finite path bijection identifies each positive prefix; absMax attainment gives strict reverse implication and sourceMaximum_le_iff gives forward pointwise domination. The n=0 conventions are not equated."
    },
    {
      "id": "A03",
      "line": 67,
      "reason": "AE coordinate measurability closes finite squared-energy and absolute finite-sum expressions; strict comparisons and countable intersections are null measurable for arbitrary measure. No iid/moment/ordinary-measurability premise introduced."
    },
    {
      "id": "A04",
      "line": 92,
      "reason": "The sequence x-(x-a)/(j+2) remains below x and tends to x. At positive energy, sqrt is positive and yields the strict event; at zero energy actual maximum is zero and every weak event holds. The union is exactly strict union zero-energy, and they are disjoint."
    },
    {
      "id": "A05",
      "line": 137,
      "reason": "Probability of X1=0 lies in [0,1); equality1 would force X1=0 AE and second integral0. Energy0 iff all finite coordinates0; finite independence and identical laws give exact p0^n including empty product n0. Centering/third moment not consumed here."
    },
    {
      "id": "A06",
      "line": 186,
      "reason": "Slow scale implies eventual positive a and positive time. For p=0 the ratio is eventually0. For 0<p<1 the proof derives a^2*n->infinity from the slow scale, applies actual Brownian firstTerm with epsilon1/2, and bounds p^n/F(a) by (pi/2)*exp((log p/2)n)->0. All denominator divisions occur on a positive tail; no antitonicity needed."
    },
    {
      "id": "A07",
      "line": 278,
      "reason": "The same-window yj increases, weak events increase, and measure continuity plus null-measurable disjoint union yields probability(strict)+probability(energy0). Actual positive continuous Brownian F allows the quotient limit; weak IsLUB bounds the limit. Triangle inequality and monotonicity pay exactly atom/F(a). Strict image is nonempty by midpoint and bounded by the finite comparison before csSup_le/le_csSup are used."
    },
    {
      "id": "A08",
      "line": 371,
      "reason": "Uses exactly qualified weak AE iid theorem with the same fixed family, third moment, zero mean, positive second integral, antitone a and both scale limits. Zero energy is p0^n; geometric ratio vanishes. On eventual n>=1 and 0<a<1 the finite comparison squeezes strict prefix-window error to0."
    },
    {
      "id": "A09",
      "line": 408,
      "reason": "Uses only eventual n>=1 to replace the prefix event by literal sourceMaximum<x*sqrt(sourceEnergy) inside the exact same real-sSup expression. X0 remains unused; arbitrary iid and Brownian universes remain independent; no law-uniform supremum or necessity claim is made."
    }
  ],
